<h2>1. Purpose and operator</h2><p>HerMap.in is being developed as a free public-interest initiative for women in India, with humanitarian and non-commercial aims. Its mission does not imply registered NGO, trust, society, Section 8 company or tax-exempt status, nor government endorsement. The responsible operator’s legal details will be published before launch. Development and creator credits do not establish who the legal operator is.</p>
<h2>2. Current service</h2><p>The local development site accepts structured reports when intake is enabled, stores them privately, and publishes only eligible delayed aggregates after moderation. There are no public individual reports or venue ratings. You do not need a public account. Public deployment remains subject to operator details and operational/legal review.</p>
<h2>3. Emergency and information limits</h2><p>HerMap is not an emergency dispatcher, police reporting service, official crime database or professional adviser. In immediate danger in India, <a href="tel:112">call 112</a>. Using HerMap does not file a police complaint or fulfil any personal legal reporting obligation.</p><p>Community reports may be incomplete, inaccurate or biased. Moderation will check policy and privacy issues; it will not independently establish an allegation. Low counts and missing data do not establish safety. High counts do not establish that a place is dangerous. Our brand message expresses our mission; it is not a promise that every report prevents harm.</p>
<h2>4. Reporting guidelines</h2><ul>
<li>Submit honestly and in good faith. Do not fabricate, coordinate false reports, impersonate others or target an individual or business.</li>
<li>Do not include personal names, phone numbers, private or exact addresses, photographs, faces, identity documents or identifying clues about survivors, witnesses, children or accused persons. Optional venue fields are only for an organisation or public place name and its official website, subject to private review. The optional location picker lets you separately opt in to encrypted private coordinates; do not select a sensitive point that identifies a survivor or child. For online harassment, the optional account field may contain only the account involved in your direct experience; it stays encrypted and private. Do not identify a survivor or child, include real names or contact details, or organise targeting of an account.</li>
<li>Do not submit threats, harassment, hate, unlawful discrimination, defamatory allegations, intimate content, sexual exploitation material or content that infringes privacy or another person’s rights.</li>
<li>Do not claim that a crime has been legally established when it has not. Broad experience categories are for reporting context, not legal determinations.</li>
<li>Do not scrape private records, probe security, bypass rate limits or automate abusive submissions. Report security concerns responsibly to our support address.</li>
</ul><p>Reporting is initially for adults aged 18 and over. Child-related information requires additional safeguards and applicable reporting obligations; an age restriction does not remove those duties.</p>
<h2>5. Moderation, removal and complaints</h2><p>Reports do not publish immediately. The service may hold, reject or remove records that violate these terms, are too identifying, appear duplicated or abusive, or must be restricted by law. There is no entitlement to publication. Approved reports wait at least <?= PUBLICATION_DELAY_HOURS ?> hours; public groups require at least <?= PUBLIC_MIN_REPORTS ?> reports. Use your private receipt to check or delete your record.</p><p>Send privacy, misuse and correction enquiries to <a href="mailto:<?= ps_escape(SUPPORT_EMAIL) ?>"><?= ps_escape(SUPPORT_EMAIL) ?></a>. A designated grievance officer and applicable acknowledgement, resolution, urgent-content and appeal procedures must be published and supported operationally before public deployment. The interim support address is not a substitute for those obligations.</p>
<h2>6. Your information and limited permission</h2><p>You retain any rights you hold in your submission. Submitting grants only the permission necessary to receive, store, review and produce broad aggregates, subject to the privacy notice and applicable law. It does not permit selling identifying information or publishing narratives. Data is handled as described in the <a href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('privacy-policy')) ?>">privacy policy</a>.</p>
<h2>7. Free access</h2><p>Viewing the map and reporting will remain free. No payment is required to submit a report, and moderation decisions cannot be purchased.</p>
<h2>8. Third-party services and intellectual property</h2><p>Linked sites and any later payment provider have their own terms and privacy practices. Survey of India outline attribution, GeoNames postal-data attribution and open-source licences are retained. The outline is used under its stated non-commercial website-use conditions. Do not remove attribution or reuse source data contrary to its licence. HerMap’s name and artwork must not be used to impersonate the service or imply endorsement.</p>
<h2>9. Availability and responsibility</h2><p>We will take reasonable care in operating the service, but cannot guarantee continuous availability, completeness or prevention of harm. Use the information with context and your own judgement. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, waives statutory rights, or provides immunity for the operator’s unlawful conduct. A humanitarian purpose does not remove legal obligations.</p>
<h2>10. Indian law and legal requests</h2><p>The service will be operated subject to applicable Indian law, including data-protection, intermediary, security, survivor-identity, defamation and child-protection requirements where applicable. Valid legal preservation, disclosure and removal obligations will be handled through an accountable process. Indian law governs these terms, subject to mandatory rights and jurisdiction rules. A specific dispute venue will be added after the legal operator is confirmed.</p>
<h2>11. Changes</h2><p>Updated terms will show a revision date. Material changes will be communicated as required. Before launch, these draft terms must be reviewed against the actual operator, product, statutory commencement dates and current amendments.</p>
